From 8f0cce50e322a28e0eb761bfbd768c75cc070db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 20:53:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] dist-tp: add a NetworkDirect (RDMA) transport, fix
 collective boundary detection

Adds an optional NetworkDirect (Windows RDMA) data path for the
distributed tensor-parallel ring, and corrects the predicate that decides
which nodes need a cross-rank all-reduce.

NetworkDirect transport
  common/dist-comm-nd.{cpp,h}, common/dist-comm.cpp, common/CMakeLists.txt

  The ND connection is negotiated out of band over the ring sockets that
  dist-comm.cpp has already set up, so bootstrap, op_hdr framing, ring
  order and the broadcasts are unchanged; only the collective payload
  moves over NetworkDirect. A header and its payload go out as one ND
  chunk.

  Two opt-ins: -DLLAMA_DIST_TP_ND=ON -DLLAMA_DIST_TP_ND_SDK=<NetworkDirect
  checkout> at build time, LLAMA_DIST_TP_RDMA=1 at run time. Every failure
  path logs and leaves the ring on TCP.

  Payloads larger than LLAMA_DIST_TP_RDMA_MAX_BYTES (default 256 KiB) stay
  on TCP. Every rank sees the same size and takes the same branch.

  This patch supports world_size=2 only.

Collective boundary detection
  ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp

  The distributed all-reduce selected boundary nodes with a name-prefix
  whitelist. build_attn() leaves the row-parallel attention output
  projection unnamed, so on dense architectures that node matched nothing
  and was never reduced, and each rank kept only its own partial sum.

  Every node that reaches this loop is a subgraph boundary, so the
  whitelist is removed. Nodes that cannot be reduced (non-contiguous,
  unsupported type, padded size) now log a warning instead of being
  skipped silently.
